From ff961c295b7f0071a2e5239b448e513cd66d81b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:37:55 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(sim): read XZ / YZ arcs on their XY footprint in
 Boundary gouge law

Law (b)'s whole-move wall reading in Boundary mode judged straight moves
and (since #905) XY arcs along their whole trace, but an XZ / YZ (G18 /
G19) arc still answered only at its chord joints. Its XY footprint is a
line, yet the joints stand up to a chord length apart on it: an r 200
arc's joints 1.92 mm apart read a wall vertex 3.90 mm off the footprint
(90 um past a 4 mm cutter's floor) at >= 4.016 mm, so the gouge passed.

New sim::verify::arc_wall_plane reads a planar vertical arc as its exact
footprint segment (out to the coordinate's turn when the sweep passes
it, at the radius band's outer edge) and a helical one as a bounded,
padded polyline (at most MAX_ARC_CHORDS pieces; pad r d^2/8 plus the
band width), so it never reads farther than the truth. Degenerate arcs
read as the chord law cuts them; a non-finite centre fails closed.

Also from the issue: boundary_arc_walls.rs moves to crates/sim/tests
(#921), XyArc::dist_seg uses a fixed buffer instead of a per-edge Vec,
and a model-backed pin covers the reading with a part mesh.

Fixes #946

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
